    "answers": {
      "A": {
        "answer": "No. For purposes of this chapter, except in section 49l–2 of this title, the term 'State agency', used without further description, means specifically an agency designated or authorized under section 49c of this title. The supplied text does not state who designates or authorizes it or what specific powers are required beyond referencing section 49c.",
        "source_refs": [
          {
            "source": "S0",
            "passage": "F000"
          },
          {
            "source": "S0",
            "passage": "F002"
          }
        ]
      },
      "B": {
        "answer": "No. Under 29 U.S.C. 49a(7), except in section 49l–2 of this title, \"State agency\", used without further description, means an agency designated or authorized under section 49c of this title. Under section 49c, the Governor designates or authorizes the creation of the State agency in accordance with a State statute accepting the provisions of the chapter, and the agency must be vested with all powers necessary to cooperate with the Secretary under the chapter.",
        "source_refs": [
          {
